Array : Collection of premetive data type. And all data should be same in an array.

Syntax : 

data type [] array_name = new data_type[Size_of_array]

array_name : this is the reference 

new keyword use to create object in heap memory => Dynamic memory Allocation (Assigning the memory space during execution or run time.)

In C or Cpp, Array contains contiguous memory, while in Java it totally depends on jvm that it will be contiguous or not. 
Because, 
> Array obj are stored in heap memory.
> Heap objects are not continuous.
> Dynamic memory Allocation
> Hence, Array in java may not be contiguous, it depends on Jvm.

